Round complete. Both files are shipped: `impl/gen_rader.c` (2-wide paired-column engine, gated per m) and the Round gen_r8 section appended to `strategies/gen_rader.md`.

**Summary of the round:** I spent all three queued r7 items. Paired-column (2-wide) chunks share every broadcast constant between two zmm columns — the dense engine took **-25.5% at L=127** (47.2 → 35.2 ms/step; PMU counters attribute it to -23% load uops and -19% L1D replacements), plus -25% at 107, -20% at 59, -15% at 23. The rp2 even-h kernels got a three-way per-m raced boundary: unchanged ≤ m13, 1-wide with rolled fold/combine loops at m=15..24 (61 -1..4%, 73 -1..10%, 89 -9..14%), and 2-wide + natural-store-order at m≥25 (101 -5..12%, 113 -8..9%). The fully-peeled 2-wide form lost everywhere (60 KB kernels — the r7 front-end lesson at 2x width) and is written down with numbers. Every change is bit-identical per column (cmp-verified at 30 primes); all single/two-step/chain gates pass on the node; L=31 is untouched, bit-identical, and a wash. llvm-mca's icelake-server model dispatches all zmm FMA to one port — recorded as a blind spot; uiCA's install is broken (missing instrData).

**Technique ended on:** paired-column (2-wide) broadcast-sharing chunks — dense engine everywhere (-25% at 127) and 2-wide+store-order at m≥25, with rolled fold/combine on the 1-wide kernels at m=15..24. **Best wallaby-node L=31: 84.46 us/xform at B=1, 84.86 us at B=16 (bit-identical to r7). Rel L2: 4.06e-16 single, 1.78e-15 two-step, 2.56e-14 chain m=140.**
